### Banking Transactions API - sample requests
### Works with the PyCharm/IntelliJ HTTP Client and the VS Code "REST Client" extension.
### Start the API first:  ./demo/run.sh

@host = http://localhost:3000

### 1. Create a transfer (201)
# @name createTransfer
POST {{host}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccount": "ACC-12345",
  "toAccount": "ACC-67890",
  "amount": 100.50,
  "currency": "USD",
  "type": "transfer"
}

> {% client.global.set("txId", response.body.id); %}

### 2. Create a deposit (only toAccount needed)
POST {{host}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{ "toAccount": "ACC-12345", "amount": 1000, "currency": "USD", "type": "deposit" }

### 3. Create a withdrawal (only fromAccount needed)
POST {{host}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fromAccount": "ACC-12345", "amount": 200, "currency": "USD", "type": "withdrawal" }

### 4. List all transactions
GET {{host}}/transactions

### 5. Get one transaction by id
### JetBrains: txId is set by request 1. VS Code REST Client: replace with
### {{createTransfer.response.body.id}}
GET {{host}}/transactions/{{txId}}

### 6. Unknown id (404)
GET {{host}}/transactions/does-not-exist

### 7. Filter by account (sender or receiver)
GET {{host}}/transactions?accountId=ACC-12345

### 8. Filter by type
GET {{host}}/transactions?type=deposit

### 9. Filter by date range (inclusive, UTC days)
GET {{host}}/transactions?from=2024-01-01&to=2030-12-31

### 10. Combined filters
GET {{host}}/transactions?accountId=ACC-12345&type=transfer&from=2024-01-01&to=2030-12-31

### 11. Account balance (per currency)
GET {{host}}/accounts/ACC-12345/balance

### 12. Account summary (Task 4, option A)
GET {{host}}/accounts/ACC-12345/summary

### 13. Export transactions as CSV (Task 4, option C)
GET {{host}}/transactions/export?format=csv

### ---- Error cases (all 400 unless noted) ----

### 14. Negative amount + invalid currency
POST {{host}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fromAccount": "ACC-12345", "toAccount": "ACC-67890", "amount": -5, "currency": "XXX", "type": "transfer" }

### 15. More than 2 decimal places
POST {{host}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fromAccount": "ACC-12345", "toAccount": "ACC-67890", "amount": 1.234, "currency": "USD", "type": "transfer" }

### 16. Bad account format
POST {{host}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fromAccount": "12345", "toAccount": "ACC-67890", "amount": 10, "currency": "USD", "type": "transfer" }

### 17. Transfer to the same account
POST {{host}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fromAccount": "ACC-12345", "toAccount": "ACC-12345", "amount": 10, "currency": "USD", "type": "transfer" }

### 18. Missing required fields
POST {{host}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 19. Invalid filters
GET {{host}}/transactions?type=gift&from=2024-02-01&to=2024-01-01

### 20. Invalid account id
GET {{host}}/accounts/bad/balance

### 21. Unsupported export format
GET {{host}}/transactions/export?format=xml

### Rate limiting (Task 4, option D): 100 requests/minute per IP, then 429.
### Try it:  for i in $(seq 105); do curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" localhost:3000/transactions; done | sort | uniq -c
